     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Your confirmation doesn't change the issue. The problem is the dose, and the person confirming it isn't a prescriber.\n\n- **Dose:** 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg. I don't see a clinical scenario where that is appropriate. The risk is serious harm, mainly lactic acidosis.\n- **Authority:** A licensed prescriber needs to take responsibility for the order. That person, or a pharmacist, should review it.\n\n**What you can do:**\n1. Ask the treating physician or a pharmacist to review the order. If they think a different dose is right, they can enter it or tell me the dose.\n2. If a typo is likely, I can enter a standard dose, such as 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). The prescriber would need to give or confirm that dose.\n\nOnce a prescriber gives me a dose within the labeled range, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
